  "text": "Board of Elections | Craven County\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nDepartments\nServices\nCommunity\nElection Information\nVoting\nWhat's on my Ballot?\nAbsentee & Early Voting\nElection Results\nPast Abstracts/Results\n1972-1980\n1981-1990\n1991-2000\n2001-2010\n2011-2020\nBridgeton - Municipal\nCove City - Municipal\nDover - Municipal\nFirst Craven Sanitary District - Municipal\nHavelock - Municipal\nNew Bern - Municipal\nRiver Bend - Municipal\nTrent Woods - Municipal\nVanceboro - Municipal\nSpecial Elections\nVoting Equipment\nCandidate Information\nCampaign Finance\nSign Information\nInformation for Running for Office / Filing\nBuffer Zones\nMunicipal Information\nVoter Statistics\nVoter History Statistics / Data\nMaps\nJurisdiction Maps\nForms\nElected Officials Listing\nPrecinct Officials\nAppointments & Training / Compensation\nChief Judges\nJudges\nAssistants\nHome\nDepartments\nElections\nBoard of Elections\nThe Board of Elections consists of five members that are appointed every two years. Two Democrats, two Republicans, and a Chair (that is appointed by the State Auditor). The elections office mission is to ensure everyone who is eligible to vote has access to efficient, fair, and open elections in accordance with federal and state election laws.\nBoard Meetings\nRegular monthly meetings are held the first Wednesday of each month at 2 pm in the Board of Elections Training Room in the Craven County Government Administration building located at 406 Craven Street in New Bern.\nSee All 2026 Board Meeting Dates and Times\nIf you would like to be put on the agenda to speak, please follow the\nPublic Agenda Policy (PDF)\n, requests have to be made 48 hours before the scheduled meeting.\nCurrent Board Members (2025-2027)\nChair: Ross Hardeman\nDemocrat Member: Ronnie D. Lovick\nRepublican Member: Ernie Richardson IV - Secretary\nRepublican Member: Michael Speciale\nDemocrat Member: Zeda B. Trice\nPast Board Members (PDF)\nin New W\nNEW: Craven County Elections GIS Map.\nThe new map will allow users to locate their voting site and other jurisdictional information using their residential address. Please click on Election Information at the top of the blue side bar to the left of this page and then select Voting. The link for the new map will be at the top of the list along with other links to verify voting information.\nNext Election Date\nNovember 03, 2026 - General Election\nEarly Voting begins October 15, 2026 and Ends October 31, 2026\nEarly Voting Locations and Hours\nA valid photo identification is required when voting in person.\nGet details at the\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections website\n.\nElection Day Polls open at 6:30 am and close at 7:30 pm.\nYou must vote at your assigned precinct on election day, based on your\nresidential address, to receive your correct ballot.\nNovember 03, 2026 - UOCAVA General Election Notice\nANY FURTHER UPDATES WILL BE POSTED HERE\nVoter History\nHistory in any election is not seen on your voter record until after the county has had their canvass meeting for the election.\nRegistration Repair Project\nThe\nRegistration Repair Project\nis an effort by the State Board of Elections to collect identification numbers from registered voters who do not have an N.C. driver\u2019s license/DMV ID number or social security number in the state\u2019s voter registration database. These numbers are used to verify that registrants are who they claim to be. Voters who do not have this information in their record may need to cast a provisional ballot and provide this information the next time they vote.\nRead on\nHERE\nersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadl\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nVersion OptionsBoard of ElectionsHeadline\nfor details about the\nRegistration Repair Search Tool\n, how registered voters listed in the search tool can fix their registration, and answers to frequently asked questions.\nPolicies\nCraven County Board of Election Media Policy\nOpens a New Window.\nCraven County Board of Election Public Agenda Item Policy\nCraven County Board of Election Observer/Runner Policy\nElection Results\nResults from previous Elections can be viewed at the\nNC State Board of Elections website\n.\nContact Us\nSusan R. Williams\nDirector, CNCED\nemail Susan R. Williams\nBoard of Elections\nEmail the Board of Elections\nPhysical Address\n406 Craven Street\nNew Bern\n,\nNC\n28560\nPhone:\n(252) 636-6610\nFax: (252) 636-6687\nHours\nMonday - Friday\n8 am - 5 pm\nQuick Links\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections\nFederal Voting Assistance Program (Military and Overseas Civilians)\nView All\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nJob\nOpenings\nNotify Me\u00ae\nContact Us\nMaps\nBill Pay\nPermits\nContact Us\n406 Craven Street,\nNew Bern, NC 28560-4971\nIf you are unsure where to direct your concern, you can call the AI-supported County phone line for assistance at (252) 667-9570.\nQuick Links\nHealth Department\nSocial Services\nSheriff\nRegister of Deeds\nTax\nAnimal Adoption\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
